Add keys, set their values and change how they are managed

Usage:
  waxseal key [command]

Available Commands:
  add         Add a key; creates the secret if it does not exist
  edit        Change how a key is managed: rotation, generator, expiry, template
  set         Store a new value for a key and reseal it

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for key

Global Flags:
      --dry-run         show what would change without changing anything
      --no-color        disable colour
      --no-input        never prompt; fail if an input is missing
  -o, --output string   output format: text or json (default "text")
      --repo string     path to the repository (default ".")
      --verbose         log subprocess calls and debug detail to stderr
  -y, --yes             answer yes to confirmations

Use "waxseal key [command] --help" for more information about a command.
